.*
!.gitignore
!.envrc
!.github
!.semgrep
!.pre-commit-config.yaml
# Share Cursor project rules (AI-guidance conventions) with every clone. The
# leading `.*` above otherwise ignores the whole .cursor tree. Only rules/ is
# re-included; .cursormemory.md and other local .cursor state stay ignored.
!.cursor/
!.cursor/rules/
!.cursor/rules/*.mdc
__pycache__
**/7-Zip
**/*.msi
**/*.msi*.log
**/centaur.tar.gz
**/Win32DiskImager-1.0.0-binary.zip
**/raspberryPi_imager_latest.exe
**/RaspberryPi_imager
**/Win32DiskImager
**/centaur.img
**/.toggled

# Ignore all build output directories (meson, cmake, ninja, etc.)
# The project scripts are now in scripts/, not build/
**/build/

# React web-app
**/web-app/node_modules/
**/web-app/dist/
# Stray npm artifacts at the repo root. There is no package.json here; the only
# frontend project lives in src/universalchess/web-app. Running `npm install`
# with the repo root as the working directory makes npm walk up, find no
# package.json, and write an empty package-lock.json (and node_modules) named
# after this folder. These leading-slash patterns are anchored to the repo root,
# so the real, tracked src/universalchess/web-app/package-lock.json is unaffected.
/package-lock.json
/node_modules/
# Built bundle staged for deploy/packaging (produced by scripts/build.sh and
# deploy-to-pi.sh; never committed - it is generated from web-app/).
src/universalchess/web/react-app/

# Release signing private keys. The PUBLIC keyring
# (packaging/deb-root/opt/universalchess/keys/release-signing.gpg) is deliberately
# tracked and ships in the package. The private half is exported to configure the
# RELEASE_SIGNING_KEY CI secret, and committing it would let anyone sign an update
# that every board accepts as genuine. These patterns cover the names that export
# produces; they do not replace reviewing what is staged.
*secret-key*.asc
*secret-keys*.asc
*private-key*.asc
*private*.gpg
secring.*
